{
  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates the variance of the lotteries and prefers the one with the smaller variance. To compute variance, we need the outcomes and their probabilities. For a lottery with outcome x with probability p and 0 with probability (1-p), the variance is: Var = p * x². \n\nLottery A: 3000 € with 0.2% (0.002) probability → variance = 0.002 * (3000)² = 0.002 * 9,000,000 = 18,000\nLottery B: 6000 € with 0.1% (0.001) probability → variance = 0.001 * (6000)² = 0.001 * 36,000,000 = 36,000\n\nThus, A has a smaller variance (18,000) than B (36,000). The decision reason therefore prefers A. The information relevant to the decision reason is available and can be derived from the lotteries' outcomes and probabilities.",
